    "question": "Bob bought 2 show dogs for $250.00 each to breed as a side business.  The female just had a litter of 6 puppies.  If he sells each puppy for $350.00, what is his total profit?",
    "gold": "1600",
    "answer": "He bought 2 dogs for $250.00 each so they costs 2*250 = $<<2*250=500.00>>500.00\nHe sells each of the 6 puppies for $350.00 so he'll make 6*350 = $<<6*350=2100.00>>2,100.00\nHe made $2,100 on the puppies but spent $500.00 to buy the dogs so his total profit is 2,100-500 = $<<2100-500=1600.00>>1,600.00\n#### 1600"
